   "title": "Are Child Car Seats Better Than Seat Belts?",
   "hook": "Parents spend money, time and anxiety on child car seats, but crash data suggested that, for kids past toddler age, a plain adult seat belt did about as well at preventing deaths.",
   "source": "SuperFreakonomics — Steven Levitt & Stephen Dubner (Ch. 4, \"The Fix Is In, and It's Cheap and Simple\")",
   "book": "SuperFreakonomics",
