   "hook": "Pay has less to do with how hard or how well you work than with how much value your work creates for someone else, and how many people are competing to do it.",
   "source": "The Economic Naturalist — Robert H. Frank (Ch. 3, \"Why Equally Talented Workers Often Earn Different Salaries and Other Mysteries of the World of Work\")",
   "book": "The Economic Naturalist",
