   "title": "Lincoln's Angry Letter That Was Never Sent",
   "hook": "Lincoln wrote a furious letter to the general who let Lee escape after Gettysburg, then put it away, because he had learned decades earlier, nearly at the point of a sword, what criticism really does.",
   "source": "How to Win Friends and Influence People — Dale Carnegie (Part 1, Ch. 1, \"If You Want to Gather Honey, Don't Kick Over the Beehive\")",
   "book": "How to Win Friends and Influence People",
   "concepts": [
    "empathy-and-listening",
    "ego-and-humility",
    "candor-and-feedback"
   ],
