   "title": "Harlan, Kentucky: The Feuds Herders Left Behind",
   "hook": "A Kentucky mountain town tore itself apart in a decades-long family feud, and Gladwell traces the violence to the herding habits of ancestors who had left Britain centuries earlier, habits that still show up in the hormones of college students today.",
   "source": "Outliers — Malcolm Gladwell (Ch. 6, \"Harlan, Kentucky\")",
