   "title": "Your Social Security Number Sets Your Price",
   "hook": "MIT students who wrote down the last two digits of their Social Security number before an auction bid far more when those random digits were high, and their bids still looked perfectly logical.",
   "source": "Predictably Irrational — Dan Ariely (Ch. 2, \"The Fallacy of Supply and Demand\")",
   "book": "Predictably Irrational",
   "concepts": [
    "predictable-irrationality",
    "intuition-and-snap-judgments"
   ],
