   "title": "Naked Economics: Undressing the Dismal Science",
   "hook": "Strip away the graphs and equations and economics turns out to be a set of plain, powerful ideas about incentives, information and trade that explain why rhinos vanish, why you trust McDonald's on a strange highway and why some countries are rich while others stay poor.",
   "source": "Naked Economics — Charles Wheelan",
