   "title": "Start-up Nation: The Story of Israel's Economic Miracle",
   "hook": "A tiny country with no natural resources, hostile neighbors and constant war ends up producing more start-ups per person than anywhere on Earth, and the reasons have more to do with culture, the army and immigrants than with luck.",
   "source": "Start-up Nation — Dan Senor & Saul Singer",
   "book": "Start-up Nation",
