   "title": "SuperFreakonomics: Global Cooling, Patriotic Prostitutes, and Why Suicide Bombers Should Buy Life Insurance",
   "hook": "An economist and a journalist go hunting through sex work, hospital wards, bank records, crash labs and volcano clouds to show that people respond to incentives, that the comfortable story is often wrong, and that the biggest problems frequently have cheap, simple fixes nobody wants to hear about.",
