   "title": "Talking to Strangers: What We Should Know About the People We Don't Know",
   "hook": "We assume we can read strangers from their faces and that they are probably telling the truth, and those two habits, plus our blindness to the places where behaviour happens, explain disasters from Munich to a Texas roadside.",
   "source": "Talking to Strangers — Malcolm Gladwell",
   "book": "Talking to Strangers",
   "concepts": [],
