   "title": "The Undercover Economist",
   "hook": "Start with the price of a cup of coffee and follow the money far enough, and you can explain supermarket tricks, traffic jams, used cars, stock-market bubbles, spectrum auctions, and why Cameroon stayed poor while China grew rich.",
   "source": "The Undercover Economist — Tim Harford",
   "book": "The Undercover Economist",
